<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- English text for Unminute.admx (#111 slice A5). -->
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
                           xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0"
                           xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Unminute</displayName>
  <description>Managed settings for Unminute, the local meeting transcription app.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="Unminute">Unminute</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_Unminute">Unminute releases after 0.4.3, on Windows 10 or 11</string>

      <string id="AllowModelDownloads">Allow model downloads in the app</string>
      <string id="AllowModelDownloads_Help">Enabled or not configured: users can download and repair speech and speaker models in Setup and Downloads.

Disabled: the app refuses downloads and shows "Ask your IT team". Use this when IT installs the models, so the app never needs the network (a models package for Intune is planned).</string>

      <string id="AllowGpuComponent">Allow the graphics card components</string>
      <string id="AllowGpuComponent_Help">Enabled or not configured: on computers with a supported NVIDIA card, users can download the graphics card components into their profile and use them: "Graphics card acceleration" (about 2 GB of PyTorch and CUDA libraries, from download-r2.pytorch.org) for speaker identification, and "Graphics card for Whisper" (about 0.6 GB of NVIDIA's cuBLAS library, from files.pythonhosted.org) for Whisper transcription.

Disabled: neither component can be downloaded or used; speaker identification and transcription run on the processor.</string>

      <string id="AllowMicrophoneRecording">Allow microphone recording</string>
      <string id="AllowMicrophoneRecording_Help">Enabled or not configured: users can turn on microphone recording in Settings.

Disabled: microphone recording is off and cannot be turned on, and a recording in progress is stopped and saved when the app next reads the policy (within 15 minutes). Recordings can still be imported.</string>

      <string id="AllowLidOverride">Allow keeping a recording going with the lid closed</string>
      <string id="AllowLidOverride_Help">Enabled or not configured: users can turn on "Keep recording when the lid is closed" in Settings. While a recording is open, Unminute then sets the active power plan's lid action to "Do nothing" (plugged in and on battery) and puts the original values back when the recording ends, or at the next start after a crash. It never changes the lid action where Group Policy or Intune sets it.

Disabled: the setting cannot be turned on, and a change already in force is put back when the app next reads the policy.</string>

      <string id="RequireRecordingConsent">Confirm before each recording that everyone has been told</string>
      <string id="RequireRecordingConsent_Help">Enabled or not configured: before each microphone recording, the person recording confirms that everyone in the meeting has been told that it is being recorded, and why. The recording starts only after they tick that statement and select Start recording. The confirmation is a window the app draws outside its web page, so the page cannot answer it.

Disabled: recordings start without this confirmation. Use this only if the firm makes sure of it another way.</string>

      <string id="AllowWatchedFolders">Allow watched folders</string>
      <string id="AllowWatchedFolders_Help">Enabled or not configured: users can choose folders that the app checks for new recordings.

Disabled: no new watched folders can be added and existing ones are not checked. From when the app next reads the policy (within 15 minutes), recordings already found in them are not imported until the policy allows watched folders again; the one being copied in at that moment finishes.</string>

      <string id="AllowDeleteOriginals">Allow deleting original recordings from watched folders</string>
      <string id="AllowDeleteOriginals_Help">Enabled or not configured: for a watched folder, a user may allow the app to delete an original recording after its transcript is reviewed (only if it is exactly the file that was imported).

Disabled: that permission cannot be given, and originals are never deleted, including for folders where it was given before. A deletion in a synced folder (OneDrive, SharePoint) also deletes the file for everyone the folder is shared with.</string>

      <string id="AllowNetworkSources">Allow recordings on network drives</string>
      <string id="AllowNetworkSources_Help">Disabled or not configured: recordings on mapped network drives, or reached through a symbolic link, are refused; users copy them to the computer first. Synced folders such as OneDrive are not affected.

Enabled: such recordings can be imported with Import or by dragging them onto the window. Opening them connects to the file server with the user's Windows credentials. Users open them through the mapped drive letter; a \\server\share path chosen directly is still refused. Watched folders must still be on the computer.</string>

      <string id="HandoffFilenameIncludesTitle">Suggest the meeting title as the handoff file name</string>
      <string id="HandoffFilenameIncludesTitle_Help">Disabled or not configured: Save suggests "Meeting transcript" with the date and time, because meeting titles often name the client and file names are recorded in many places (recent items, search indexes, sync logs).

Enabled: Save suggests the meeting title, except when speaker names are being replaced.</string>

      <string id="ClipboardClearMinutes">Clear the app's handoff copy from the clipboard</string>
      <string id="ClipboardClearMinutes_Help">Enabled: a handoff copied with the app's Copy button is removed from the clipboard after this many minutes (1 to 1440), and when the app closes, unless something else was copied in the meantime. Time the computer spends asleep counts.

Disabled, not configured or 0: the app never clears the clipboard.</string>

      <string id="HandoffDefaultFolder">Starting folder for saved handoffs</string>
      <string id="HandoffDefaultFolder_Help">Enabled: the handoff Save dialog starts in this folder, for example a client files location. Use a full path that starts with a drive letter; a mapped drive is fine, but \\server\share paths are not accepted. Environment variables such as %USERPROFILE% are expanded. Users can still choose another folder.

Not configured, or a folder that does not exist: the dialog starts in its usual place.</string>

      <string id="AllowHandoffAssistant">Allow "Copy and open" on the Hand off page</string>
      <string id="AllowHandoffAssistant_Help">Enabled or not configured: the Hand off page's main button copies the prompt and transcript, then asks Windows to open the assistant's web address in the user's default browser. By default it is "Copy and open ChatGPT", opening https://chatgpt.com/; set "Hand off assistant name" and "Hand off assistant address" to use another. The user signs in, pastes, checks and sends: Unminute sends nothing, never puts transcript text in the address and never types into the browser. The page reminds users to paste only into the organisation's business account; Unminute cannot check which account is signed in.

Disabled: the button is not shown, and the page offers Copy prompt and transcript, Copy prompt only and Save Markdown as before. A value that is not 0 or 1, or a policy key that cannot be read, also turns it off.</string>

      <string id="HandoffAssistantName">Hand off assistant name</string>
      <string id="HandoffAssistantName_Help">The name shown on the button, as "Copy and open [name]", and in its messages, for example Copilot. 1 to 30 characters: letters, digits, single spaces and . - &amp; ' ( ) +.

Set this together with "Hand off assistant address". If only one of the two is set, or either is not valid, the button is not shown: Unminute does not fall back to ChatGPT. Not configured (both): ChatGPT at https://chatgpt.com/. Setting this policy to Disabled is expected to remove the value, which counts as not configured.</string>

      <string id="HandoffAssistantUrl">Hand off assistant address</string>
      <string id="HandoffAssistantUrl_Help">The web address opened after copying, for example https://assistant.example.org/chat (an illustration, not a real service). It must start with https:// in lower case, followed by a host name in lower case of at least two parts (not an IP address or a single name such as localhost, and no trailing dot), with no user name, password or port other than 443, then an optional path and query. At most 300 characters. Internationalised host names must be written in their xn-- form. Users see the host name under the button.

Unminute fails closed: any of these anywhere in the address makes it not valid, and the button is not shown: an @ (also in the path or query, so a link that carries an email address cannot be used), #, a space, tab, line break or other control character, a non-ASCII character, the characters " ' &lt; &gt; \ ^ ` { | }, a % not followed by two hexadecimal digits, %00 to %1F and %7F, a : with no port number after the host, and a ? with nothing after it.

Set this together with "Hand off assistant name". If only one of the two is set, or either is not valid, the button is not shown: Unminute does not fall back to ChatGPT. Not configured (both): ChatGPT at https://chatgpt.com/. Setting this policy to Disabled is expected to remove the value, which counts as not configured.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="ClipboardClearMinutes">
        <decimalTextBox refId="ClipboardClearMinutes" defaultValue="10">Minutes</decimalTextBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="HandoffDefaultFolder">
        <textBox refId="HandoffDefaultFolder">
          <label>Folder</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="HandoffAssistantName">
        <textBox refId="HandoffAssistantName">
          <label>Name</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="HandoffAssistantUrl">
        <textBox refId="HandoffAssistantUrl">
          <label>Address (https://)</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
